TANF 103-6 Voter Registration Supersedes: TANF 103-6 (1/1/06) Reference: National Voter’s Registration Act of 1993; MCA 13-2-221 Overview: The National Voter’s Registration Act (NVRA) and §13 2-221, MCA, require DPHHS to offer voter registration assistance to individuals who apply for public assistance, seek redetermination or who change an address. VOTER REGISTRATION ASSISTANCE: The law requires DPHHS to offer the following voter registration assistance: 1. The opportunity to register to vote; 2. Assistance in completing a Montana Voter Registration Application (MT-VRA); and 3. Collecting complete MT-VRA’s from clients.

The law requires DPHHS to provide individuals who do not decline voter registration: 1. Blank MT-VRA form; 2. Assistance in completing the MT-VRA; and 3. Collecting completed MT-VRA forms.

DPHHS is also required to: 1. Provide specific notices to individuals regarding their NVRA rights; 2. Accept and submit completed MT-VRAs to the election administrator in the individual’s county of residence; and 3. Report information to the Montana Secretary of State regarding the actions DPHHS undertakes to fulfill its duties under the NVRA and § 13-2-221, MCA. STAFF RESPONSIBILITIES: No DPHHS employee may: 1. Seek to influence an applicant’s political preference or decisions; 2. Display on State property any political preference or party allegiance; 3. Make any statement or take any action to discourage an applicant from registering to vote;

